WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.470
Some nuclei barely exist.

2
00:00:02.520 --> 00:00:08.480
Polonium-214 has a half-life
of just 164 microseconds.

3
00:00:08.530 --> 00:00:10.650
Others hardly seem to change.

4
00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:16.170
Uranium-238 has a half-life
of 4.5 billion years.

5
00:00:16.220 --> 00:00:20.360
Either way, nothing outside
speeds them up or slows them down.

6
00:00:20.410 --> 00:00:24.170
Temperature, pressure and
chemistry make no difference.

7
00:00:24.220 --> 00:00:29.840
So if half a sample decays in an hour,
why isn't the rest gone an hour later?

8
00:00:29.890 --> 00:00:34.900
In this mission, you'll find out what it
means for decay to be random and spontaneous.

9
00:00:34.950 --> 00:00:37.680
Then you'll work out how
many nuclei are left,

10
00:00:37.730 --> 00:00:41.710
and how many have decayed,
after several whole half-lives.

11
00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:45.790
Your mission: explain why the
second hour doesn't finish the job.
